Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 05:36:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10742/11362] Measure the quarantine tax: 46% of today's
 experiment output is flagged

Instances 6 and 7 of the data-borne marker defect landed 28 minutes apart this
morning. exp6871, substrate deterministic CPU primary-receipt opportunity
reconstruction at 2.47s, and exp6872, deterministic CPU bounded reliability-state
online update simulation at 3.63s. Neither carries a compute marker in any
declaration field, so neither touched a model.

Counting artifacts written since midnight rather than repeating a raw tally: 13
experiment artifacts, 6 stamped flagged_adversarial, 4 of those data-borne false
positives. Forty-six percent of the day's output is quarantined.

The proportion is the point. A few mislabelled artifacts is a correctness problem;
half a day's output excluded from capstones and headline aggregation is a throughput
problem. It also compounds with the capstone findings already filed, since the same
defect over-excludes at the gate and under-enforces at the consumer -- the last four
capstones lack the check that would honour the quarantine.

The caveat is recorded with the number: it counts by mtime, so a rewritten older
artifact would be included and a mid-retry task excluded, and 13 is a small
denominator. The direction is what is being claimed, not the exact percentage.

